# Email Templates

Email templates allow you to create reusable, personalized communications for your event guests. Templates support both English and Arabic with automatic right-to-left formatting.

## Overview

The email template system helps you:

- Create consistent, professional communications
- Personalize emails with guest and event information
- Support bilingual communications (English/Arabic)
- Organize templates by type for different purposes

## Template Types

Each template is assigned a type that indicates its purpose:

### Invitation

Initial event invitations sent to guests, typically including event details and an RSVP link.

### Reminder

Follow-up emails for guests who haven't responded, encouraging them to submit their RSVP.

### Confirmation

Sent after a guest confirms their attendance, often including event logistics and what to expect.

### Declined Acknowledgment

A courteous response when a guest declines, thanking them and leaving the door open for future events.

### Update

Communications about changes to event details, schedule modifications, or important announcements.

### Cancellation

Notifications when an event is cancelled or a guest's invitation is withdrawn.

### Custom

For any communication that doesn't fit the standard categories, such as special instructions or personal messages.

## Bilingual Support

Every template can have both English and Arabic versions:

- **English (EN)** - Primary content displayed to English-speaking guests
- **Arabic (AR)** - Arabic translation with automatic right-to-left (RTL) formatting

You can set a default language for each template, which determines which version is used when no preference is specified.

{% callout type="info" %}
Arabic content automatically receives RTL text direction and appropriate font styling when previewed or sent.
{% /callout %}

## Default Templates

Mark a template as "default" to automatically use it for a specific type:

- One default per template type per event
- Default templates are used when sending automated communications
- You can still manually select a different template when needed

## Getting Started

Learn how to create templates in the [Creating Templates](/docs/email-templates/creating-templates) guide, and discover how to personalize content in the [Using Variables](/docs/email-templates/using-variables) guide.
